# Measured off art/back.jpg (exdoc, plate 3, manual from the hero,
# nothing lettered on it), as fractions of its width (728px): the
# colophon between 0.54 and 0.87, centred on the width; the band from
# 1.238 (0.880 of the height), 0.169 tall, a violet near black — a
# short band, so the strip is one row, the install command beside the
# name. The plate brought its lines of light brighter and closer than
# asked, and its top lighter; no frame on it, so the screenshots start
# near the top of the face, two frames at the shots' own proportion
# (900x780). The front left its era and set its lockup in a plain
# classical serif, so the back takes the editorial faces, not the big
# box's extruded black; the accent is that lockup's pale gilt.
FRAMES="0.075,0.07,0.40,0.347 0.525,0.07,0.40,0.347"
FRAME_RULE="#15101F,6,#F7C5A2,2"
CAPTION_Y=0.44
HEAD_Y=0.51
PANEL=""
BLURB_Y=0.585
FEAT_Y=0.80
REQ_Y=1.08
NAME_Y=1.26
INSTALL_ROW=beside
NAME_POINT=0.019
NAME_KERN=0.001
INSTALL_POINT=0.014
ERA=editorial
ACCENT="#F7C5A2"
